                <pb facs="0393" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg383"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 10.</seg></opener>
                <head>Sir F. Rogers to Mr. Hammond.—(Received February 25.)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Downing Street,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 25, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to previous correspondence
                    on this subject, I am directed by the Duke of Newcastle to transmit to you, for
                    the consideration of Earl Russell, the accompanying copies of two despatches
                    received from the governor of the Cape of Good Hope reporting the circumstances
                    connected with the seizure of the Tuscaloosa by the colonial government.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK ROGERS.</signed></closer>












